<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <style>
    .r8-hero-lede { text-align: left; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .r8-hero-lede:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .r8-hero-cta { margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center; }
  </style>

  <div class="r8-hero">
    <h1 class="r8-hero-title">It's Still Just Math</h1>
    <p class="r8-hero-lede">
      This is a running collection of short, hands-on walkthroughs connecting math most of us haven't
      touched since school to the systems we work with every day: optimization, rate limiters,
      autoscalers, search, all of it.
    </p>
    <p class="r8-hero-lede">
      As software engineering matured, a lot of the math underneath it got abstracted away, and we're
      watching that happen all over again with AI. I think it matters to remember where these ideas come
      from, no matter how technical you are, so I want this to be for everybody. Anyone should be able to
      drop into the first topic and walk away able to solve a simple problem themselves.
    </p>
    <p class="r8-hero-lede">
      Every bit of math on these pages is worked out by hand, by me, which means it will occasionally be
      wrong. The worked examples sit behind a button so you can skip them, or click through and check my
      work.
    </p>
    <p class="r8-hero-lede">
      The idea came from two places. First, I need the Elixir practice. Second, I'm in the final stretch
      of my own education and need to review all of this anyway, so if I'm up past midnight cursing a
      math problem, I might as well write down what I learn and share it.
    </p>
    <p class="r8-hero-lede">
      Lastly, I love math, or at least the idea of it. There's a suggestions button up at the top of this
      page, use it. I don't care if it's basic trigonometry or partial differential equations, whatever
      gets the most requests gets written up. Promise. Well kinda, I'm not doing it if it's too hard.
    </p>

    <div class="r8-hero-cta">
      <.button navigate={~p"/topics"} variant="primary">
        See the full table of contents <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </.button>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
